From 9145e2b2ade8de3d7b710e2e0a09cd4339492cd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:31:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: the PIC32CM analog comparators (AC U2245)

mchp-ac-u2245 models the AC of the PIC32CM JH01 (four comparators) and
MC00 (two), from two probe rounds on MC00 rev A1 silicon (firmware/hello
APP=acprobe, acprobe2): AIN pads (the board's "ain", or VDDANA/GND while
the PORT drives the pad), VSCALE, INTREF and the DAC (only with IOEN);
COMPCTRL locked by its own ENABLE; start-up and single-shot times; 60 mV
hysteresis; INTSEL flags with no edge flag on the first comparison;
window pairs, WIN flags on entering the WINTSEL region; COMP and WIN
event outputs, SOC start events and the CMP pads. Continuous comparators
compare on every access and when an input changes: the DAC U2214 now
notifies listeners, and the AIN pads are watched. A start-up that is due
completes on the next access, so polling firmware sees silicon's timing
without icount.

The ADC U2247 also reads PORT-driven pads. The SoC fills a model's
"<group>-pads" property from the device's signals, and pushes its new
"vddana" property to every analog model's "vdd". The MC00 board takes
vcc=<mV>, its VCC_SEL jumper. qtest pic32cm-ac-test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
